#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Measure how much of a page's DOM a browse snapshot actually exposes.

One number per site — controls in the snapshot over controls in the DOM — with
the known excuses attached (truncated, dialog-scoped, no DOM controls). A site
that renders controls and exposes none of them is the interesting bucket.

    browse-coverage                      # the built-in list
    browse-coverage --urls sites.json    # [{"name": ..., "url": ...}, ...]
    browse-coverage --settle 10 --json out.json

It reads only: no clicks, no typing.
"""

